WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.968
-It's so good to see you.
-Much love, much love.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.501
-Is this true, by the way,
that you started --

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:05.901
Before acting,
you started doing stand-up?

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:08.200
You were doing comedy?
-Yeah, I was doing comedy.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.634
But, I mean, I was doing comedy
even back in junior high school,

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.467
'Cause -- I don't know --
I got beat up a lot.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.934
I was a beat-up magnet
for bullies.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.300
-Oh, really?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.934
-Oh, my God, they were always
after me for something.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.400
They were like, "Yo, John,
give me your sneakers."

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.133
Yo, John,
give me your lunch money."

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.634
And I was like, "Come on, man.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.834
What if I do a voice for you,
and you stop beating me up?

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.067
How about if I do,
you know, Ricky Ricardo?"

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.334
[ As Ricardo ] Heh-heh-heh!

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:29.901
Don't beat up, John.
You don't do that, please."

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:30.934
Heh-heh-heh!"

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.133
-No, no, no.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.534
Or how about Jerry Lewis?

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.834
"Don't hit me, don't hit me,
Crazy Louie."

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.400
You know, and then I'd be like,
"Whoa, whoa, Dean!

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.734
Whoa, whoa.
You won't hurt John, would you?"

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.367
-"You wouldn't do that to John."

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.300
-"Oh, my God, he does it well."
-"You do it as well, too."

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.701
-"No, not as good."
[ Laughs ]

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.334
-Oh, my God.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.801
-Oh, my God,
did they beat you up, too?

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.334
-Yeah, of course.
I got bullied all the time.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.801
But you have one of
the coolest first roles ever

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:54.534
that I think anyone
that's ever been on the show.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.834
You were an extra --
an extra extra extra.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.334
-Oh, you've got a picture?
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.467
You were in Madonna's
"Borderline" video.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.667
-Well, barely.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:05.634
I'm so in the background,
I'm blurry.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.100
-Yeah, so, you're --

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.300
-In the red tracksuit.
-Wow! That is rad.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.334
-Oh, my God,
I was so excited to be there

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.334
because I had heard that
Madonna liked Latin guys.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:18.033
So this is like Latin Tinder
back in the day.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.367
You just show up to
a Madonna music video...

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.834
-And hope for the best.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:25.000
-...and, you know, maybe you'll
be in the limo and whatnot.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.434
-Did it happen?
-No, man.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.601
The producer came up to me,

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:28.734
"No, John,
you're not going over there."

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:29.968
Gave me a sandwich
and a pat on the back,

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.267
and I went home.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.934
-You didn't even get paid?
-No, I didn't get paid.

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:34.067
-At least you got
a sandwich out of it.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.067
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, something.

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.234
-Does Madonna --
Have you seen her since?

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.734
-Yeah, I've hung out with her
a little bit.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.000
Yeah, she's mad cool.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.434
She comes here
all the time, right?

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.634
-She does. But, so, does she
remember you from this video?

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.200
-Hell no.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.901
No, no.
I don't even try to bring it up.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.234
I was an extra
that nobody remembers.

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.367
-Now you're John Leguizamo.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.634
You're like,
"Oh, I would never do that.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:52.868
Please." Exactly, yeah.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.000
"I won a Tony.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.400
Please, yeah,
I don't do that stuff."

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.767
-I didn't start as an extra.
What are you talking about?

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:59.100
-No, I've never done that.
Well, now Madonna will see this.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.834
-Oh, you blew up my spot.
Thank you.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:02.834
-Why not?

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.033
-That's what I get
for coming here.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.167
-Can we talk about the show
on MSNBC,

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.267
"Leguizamo Does America"?

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.901
-Yes, sir. I'm going to go
around America

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.334
showing what
Latin people are like,

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.467
because we're basically
invisible everywhere,

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:14.901
even though
we're the largest ethnic group

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.601
and the oldest ethnic group
in America.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.400
Oh, yeah!

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.167
That's right. Represent.
-That's right.

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.434
-You know, and that's what's up.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.300
We're everywhere,
but not, you know,

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.734
in the media, not in movies.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.634
We're less than 2%
of the leads on film.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.000
So I'm going to talk about
all these topics

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.234
and about our food and our dance
and our music and all that.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.801
Yeah, celebrate Latin culture.
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-"Leguizamo Does America."

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:42.634
-Yes, sir.
-On MSNBC.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.801
And are you adventurous
with eating?

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:47.033
-Oh, my God,
I'm Johnny-try-anything.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.334
-You will?
-Oh, my God.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.868
I've eaten snake,
which tasted like cat food.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.367
Don't ask me how
I know what cat --

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.133
-I was going to say,
how do you know that?

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:58.234
-And turtle tastes
like throw-up from snake.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:02.467
And then I had cobra blood.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.133
-What?
-Cobra blood. I had cobra blood.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.667
-Cobra blood?
-Yeah, in Thailand.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.901
It's supposed to be, like, for,
you know, virility and whatnot.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.200
It's better than the Viagra.
Your nose doesn't swell up.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.000
-Does it -- It works?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.534
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
It did work.

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:17.801
You seem surprised.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.100
-Well, now
I'm thinking about it,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.033
I go to the bedroom
and get a pint of cobra blood.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.234
-Come on, baby.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:26.400
-Yeah, yeah. Oh, my God.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.000
-I mean, not that.
That's a snake. That's a snake.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.133
-He was doing the cobra.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.234
-He was doing the cobra.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.534
-Get your minds
out of the gutter.

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:35.634
-I mean, please.
-Geez. Frightening.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.667
-Could we talk about "The Menu,"
by the way.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:38.701
-"The Menu."

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.267
-You were phenomenal
in this movie.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.367
-Oh, thank you, man.
-The cast was great.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:43.601
The movie was great.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:44.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-The script was great.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:46.801
-Oh, it was amazing.
Amazing script.

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:50.033
The cast -- I mean,
some of the greatest actors

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.634
in American theater,
in American film --

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:55.834
Ralph Fiennes, Janet McTeer,
Reed Birney, Judith Light.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.000
Oh, my God, it was incredible.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.634
-Were you all in the same room
just acting?

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:01.501
-It was like a stage play.
We were always there 24/7.

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:02.634
I mean, you got to see
everybody act.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:05.267
And it was like
a master class in acting.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:06.701
-I think you did a master class.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.701
Watching you -- I want to zone
in and focus on you.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:12.000
-Oh, please do.
I'm not complaining.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.734
-I loved because you start off
so cocky and confident.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:15.934
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:17.367
-You know, no spoilers,
of course.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.234
But then, you kind of
get a little gross.

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:21.434
And then it's like --
Then you kind of get scary.

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:22.801
Then you're almost the hero.

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:24.534
But you're so real
and so good in this.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.200
I don't want to spoil it if
you haven't seen it.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.501
It is so well done.
-Now I want to watch it again.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.734
-Yeah, yeah.
You were really great in it.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.200
-Yeah, I've got to see that.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.501
-I just want to say thank you
so much for coming on.

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:35.834
And you were phenomenal.

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.601
Anyone who hasn't seen
John Leguizamo in "The Menu,"

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:38.834
watch this right now.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:39.968
I want to show a clip.
-Oh, yeah, show a clip.

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:42.033
-Here's John Leguizamo in
"The Menu."

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.901
-Do you need assistance
finding your seat?

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:45.267
-There's a finger. The finger.
There's a finger right there.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.400
-The man is screaming in pain.
What's...

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.868
-Please, sit.

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.334
-[ Laughs ]
-It's not funny, lady.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.767
Jesus Christ!
-It's all part of the menu.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:58.334
-Oh, my God.
-This is real, isn't it?

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.634
I can't do it.
I can't -- I can't do --

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:01.834
-Then why don't you go
talk to him.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.767
Go talk to him,
because you know him, right?

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.367
-I made that up.

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:06.801
-Why?

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:09.000
-Because I'm
a name-dropping whore.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.133
That's why, okay?

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:12.901
-John Leguizamo!

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:16.200
"The Menu" is available on
Blu-ray and digital.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.100
We'll be right back with a
performance from SG Lewis.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.300
Stick around, everybody.
-Yeah.

